PRIVACY POLICY FOR ORBIT PATH: SPACE TRAVELLER
Last Updated: May 8, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Orbit Path: Space Traveller ("we," "us," or "our") collects, uses, and discloses information about you when you use our mobile application on iOS.

1. Information We Collect
To provide a smooth interstellar gaming experience, we collect limited data. We do not request access to your contacts, camera, or precise GPS location.

a. Usage Data & Game Analytics: * Purpose: To improve gameplay balance, fix bugs, and optimize performance. We may track high scores, level progression, and crash reports.

Processing: This data is aggregated and anonymous. It helps us understand which levels are too difficult or if the game crashes on specific device models.

b. Device Information: * Purpose: We collect basic information such as device model, OS version, and language settings to ensure the game renders correctly on your screen.

2. Third-Party Advertising & Tracking
To keep this space journey free for everyone, we use third-party advertising networks, such as Google AdMob.

a. Identifiers (IDFA): With your explicit permission, we may access your device’s Advertising Identifier (IDFA) to show ads that might interest you (e.g., other strategy games or tech products).

b. App Tracking Transparency (ATT): In compliance with Apple’s iOS requirements, the game will ask for your permission to track activity across other apps.

Your Choice: You can select "Ask App Not to Track."

Effect of Declining: You will still see ads, but they will be generic and not based on your interests. The core game experience remains fully accessible.

3. Data Sharing and Disclosure
We do not sell your personal data. We only share anonymous, aggregated data with service providers (like Google AdMob or Firebase) for the following purposes:

Displaying advertisements.

Analyzing game performance and stability.

For more details on how our partners handle data, please review: Google Privacy & Terms.

4. Children’s Privacy
Orbit Path: Space Traveller is intended for a general audience. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under the age of 13. If you believe we have inadvertently collected such information, please contact us immediately, and we will delete it.

5. Security
The majority of your game data (like unlocked levels and ships) is stored locally on your device. We implement reasonable industry-standard measures to protect any data transmitted for analytics or advertising.

6. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this policy to reflect changes in our game or legal requirements. We will notify you by updating the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page.

